38.steps:
1.Start packet capture on the firewall;
2.Click the add button on the Network Monitor Policies page;
3.On the pop up window, enter a policy name say Ping Probe;
4.Select Ping(ICMP) as the probe type;
5.Create a reachable host as the probe target, leave other fields as default;
6.Click the ok button; verify the policy is added with Yellow pseudo-LED.
7.Wait about 30 seconds or less, verify the led turns green;
8.Disconnect the egress interface, wait for about 30 seconds, verify the led turns red.

38.result:
 There should be an echo ping request sent out from the egress interface every 5 seconds, and every request sends out, the count of probes send will increase;
When the host is reachable, there should be same reply return on the egress interface,   and every reply receives, the count of Responses received will increase; After three intervals, Led should turn green and the target status change to Up;
When the host is unreachable, only the count of probes send will increase every 5 seconds, Led should turn red and the target status change to Down.

