40.steps:
1.Start packet capture on the firewall;
2.Click the add button on the Network Monitor Policies page;
3.On the pop up window, enter a policy name say ping explicit;
4.Select a host behind the router as the probe target;
5.Select Ping-explicit as the probe type;
6.Select interface x0 as the outbound interface;
7.Create an address object of the routers interface 0/1 as the next hop gateway;
8.Leave other fields as default, then click the ok button;
9.Wait about 30 seconds or less, verify the led turns green;
10.Change the next hop gateway, select Select an address object and click OK. Wait for several seconds, verify the led turns red.

40.result:
 There should be an echo ping request sent out from x0 interface every 5 seconds, and the count of probes send will increase every request sends out;
When the target is reachable, there should be same reply return on the egress interface,   and every reply receives, the count of Responses received will increase; After three intervals, Led should turn green and the target status change to Up;
Target will become unreachable when no gateway is chosen. Then led should turn red and the target status change to Down.

